From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:27:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: sun50i-di300: pass copy_frame_flags on 6.18

6.18's v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata() takes copy_frame_flags; the driver
is written for a kernel whose call has none and copies the flags.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
index 98f97cc4f..c995e8b64 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-di300/sun50i-di300.c
@@ -210,8 +210,8 @@ static void deinterlace_device_run(void *priv)
 	ctx->dst0 = dst0;
 	ctx->dst1 = dst1;
 
-	v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata(src, dst0);
-	v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata(src, dst1);
+	v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata(src, dst0, true);
+	v4l2_m2m_buf_copy_metadata(src, dst1, true);
 
 	next = vb2_dma_contig_plane_dma_addr(&src->vb2_buf, 0);
 	curr = ctx->prev[0] ?
-- 
2.47.3

